CLINICAL REASONING SUMMARY

The patient presented with acute, profound sensory overwhelm, sudden physical disconnection, and migrating somatic pain. Telephone triage appropriately identified the urgent need to rule out an acute neurological event, systemic infection, or severe acute metabolic derangement given the sudden cognitive 'spacing out' and generalized pain. Immediate on-site clinical assessment was strictly necessary to perform a thorough neurological and physical examination. The ruling out of focal neurological deficits and systemic infection confirmed the patient's physical safety, but the severity of the sensory and cognitive distress dictated that delaying assessment until the next in-hours period posed a high risk of acute psychological decompensation and autonomic hyperarousal. This urgent intervention satisfies MBS Items 585-600 criteria.

